## the deck's ("Handling Objections", WALKAWAY Webinar Series 4), condensed;
## the bare ones are everybody else's. savings and line_of_credit are never
## raised outright - asking "how would you make the payments?" flushes them out.
const KNOWN_OBJECTIONS := [
	&"walkaway_too_expensive", &"walkaway_no_thanks", &"walkaway_dont_need",
	&"walkaway_savings", &"walkaway_line_of_credit", &"walkaway_work_coverage",
	&"walkaway_lots_of_insurance", &"walkaway_wont_qualify",
	&"walkaway_buy_outright",
	&"walkaway_gap_too_expensive", &"walkaway_gap_insured",
	&"walkaway_gap_dont_need", &"walkaway_gap_no_thanks",
	&"too_expensive", &"dont_need", &"no_thanks"]

const DESIGN_RULE := "One library, divided by TAG, not by file. A line's tags say which pool it belongs to and are the only required match; archetype_ids, product_ids, appeal_bands and objection_ids are optional narrowings, and an empty one means any. Narrowing is additive and exclusive: a line naming karen is unavailable to everybody else, never merely less likely. Every tag must keep at least one line with NO narrowings at all - that is the fallback that stops a pool going silent, and the suite enforces it. Specific lines are WEIGHTED over generic ones, never substituted for them: one karen line must not make ten generic ones unreachable, or every karen says the same sentence for the rest of the run. The one exception is an open objection: where lines answer it, only they are drawn, because the word track written for it IS the answer. A line's `becomes` opens or moves the customer's objection when it is said. The player_* tags are YOUR lines, asked for by a card's player_dialogue_tags; on those, an archetype narrowing means who you are talking to. GENERATED by tools/build_dialogue.gd - edit the rows there, not this file."

